Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/TuxInDrive
Description: Private peer and multi-provider cloud storage client for Debian desktops
 TuxInDrive provides browser-based OAuth, automatic transfer-engine bootstrap,
 eight cloud providers plus GitHub repositories, searchable multilingual in-app documentation, English/German/French/Spanish/Arabic/Hebrew UI selection with RTL text, encrypted provider-linked profile backup and device migration, adaptive capability controls, sync-health and audit dashboards, optional Nautilus actions/status, block-delta planning, NAT/relay peer connectivity, per-file offline controls, drag-reorderable and collapsible synchronized-folder groups, policy-aware transfers, role-based multi-peer sharing, expiring encrypted file drops, LAN/QR pairing, local-first CRDT editing, encrypted presence, structured ODT/ODS checkpoints, edit leases, multiple accounts, two-way and
 one-way synchronization, selective folders, conflict handling, tray controls,
 Tor v3 Onion Services with per-device authorization and fail-closed privacy
 policies, notifications, in-app verified updates, and files-on-demand virtual drives
 through rclone and FUSE.
